Saffrodex layered fork
======================

Saffrodex is a small downstream distribution of OpenAI Codex.
This repository keeps its downstream work as stable canonical layers instead
of continually rebasing one rolling source branch.

`layerctl` projects the repository's ordered layers onto a pinned Codex
`rust-v*` release.
The resulting Git history has the upstream release as its ancestor and one
generated commit for each Saffrodex layer, while the canonical layer history
remains stable when upstream changes.

The current product layers provide:

- `saffron.await_exec`, an event-driven wait for unified exec sessions;
- goal supervision and active-goal editing;
- current-time context for supervisor check-ins; and
- isolated Saffron persistence and recovery for scheduled supervisor wakes.

Repository layout
-----------------

```text
.github/workflows/      Canonical release automation
layers/NNNN-layer-slug/ Ordered generated commit definitions
mise.toml / mise.lock   Pinned standalone layerctl dependency
LAYERCTL.md             Layer maintenance and release operations
tools/                  Canonical repository operations
```

Layer directory names are applied in lexical order.
Their four-digit prefixes are the only ordering mechanism.
Each directory contains `layer.toml`, declaring its generated commit message
and ordered operations for patches and overlays.
The foundation manifest also pins the official Codex release tag and commit.
Multiple patch operations can contribute to one generated commit.
`layers/0000-foundation/` is the required first layer and carries changes
needed by every generated Saffrodex source tree.

Install the pinned [standalone layerctl](https://github.com/NonLogicalDev/util.layerctl)
with `mise install --locked github:NonLogicalDev/util.layerctl`.
See `LAYERCTL.md` for setup, projection, layer capture, upstream advancement,
verification, and release operations.

The default-branch workflow creates releases from a full projection:

```text
tools/release.sh [-b RELEASE_NOTES]
```

The script only dispatches that workflow.
The workflow reads the foundation source pin,
materializes the canonical layers, chooses the next Saffrodex release number,
publishes the immutable projection tag, builds each platform, and creates the
GitHub release.

See `AGENTS.md` for the complete repository operating contract.
